  "formal_scope": "Lean 4.35.0 proves, for actual r-uniform hypergraphs on Fin n, Berge copies of B_a with injective vertex and hyperedge maps, and saturation under every absent r-set, that the saturation number, defined as the least size of a saturated hypergraph on Fin n, equals ⌊a(n + 1)/((r − 1)a + 1)⌋ for all a, r ≥ 3 and n ≥ (r − 1)a + 1, together with the near-minimum structure theorem; a strict audit covers all 570 project declarations. The smaller orders, the sharpness constructions and the minimality among trees have conventional proofs.",
